 0.57}, "rating_margin": 2.29, "sigma_race": 4.7, "sigma_total": 5.29, "baseline_margin": 2.67, "analyst_adjustment": -0.07, "key_factors": ["Late polls consistently show Brown narrowly ahead, averaging roughly 2-3 points", "Prediction markets price Brown near 70% despite Ohio's Republican lean", "Husted's incumbency and state fundamentals partially offset a strong Democratic midterm environment", "Brown's large fundraising edge over the appointed incumbent"], "rationale": "The polling average puts Brown up about 2.5-3 points in the final days, and markets and most expert ratings converge on a modest Democratic edge even in a state Trump carried twice. Husted's incumbency and Ohio's Republican tilt keep this short of Likely D.", "watch": "Turnout composition in the special election — if Republican-leaning voters outperform their polling share, a one-to-two-point polling error would flip the result.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Appointed Senator Jon Husted defends the seat once held by JD Vance against former Senator Sherrod Brown in a race both parties treat as a marquee midterm contest. Ohio still leans Republican by about five points, but the 2026 environment favors Democrats, and Brown has outraised Husted substantially while drawing heavy outside opposition spending. Final polls from a wide range of pollsters show Brown ahead by one to seven points, with the consensus around two to three. Expert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets give Brown roughly a 70% chance. The race remains close enough that normal polling error could decide it, but the weight of late evidence favors Brown narrowly.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.